A||||4||Ferrari_cdn||Cleaning the taillights?||||1||
Z||000000||Ferrari_cdn||09-27-2001||08:00 PM||||When I was in the mood for cleaning everything up, inside and out, I remembered the thread about someone cleaning her taillights so I thought I would do the same, and when I unscrewed the 6 screws and took the taillights out (notchback).  I tried to pry the plastic cover off but I realize that the rubber sealant was also peeling off but some sticking to the light base and some sticking with the plastic cover.  What should I do?  I don't know if what I am doing will damage the sealant and if it will be a bad thing.  Help me out  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ferrari_2.JPG">  <BR>'84 2m4, 4 speed, 106k miles (157k km)  AIM: CanadianFiero||||reg||1
Z||000001||DXR_DAD||09-27-2001||08:15 PM||||Go ahead ICE, your ok, remove all the black sealant and replace it?  Most home improvment stores sell it, comes in a roll<BR>Gray of Black. Forgot the name? It's a puddy used to seal windows.<P><BR>DXR_DAD||||reg||14
Z||000002||Cheever3000||09-27-2001||08:18 PM||||Yeah, or a tube of silicone caulk should do fine.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||lowfunds||09-27-2001||08:20 PM||||No big deal the sealant must come off to pull it apart. Be very careful not to break any tabs. After your finished I resealed mine on the outside edge with silicone, this way if you need to take it apart again just cut the bead.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Driven Visions||09-27-2001||08:23 PM||||The Sealant is called Butyl<BR>You should be able to get it at any good auto<BR>parts store<BR>I wouldnt use silicone or you will have to break out the taillamps the next time you need to remove them<P>||||reg||1
